Package: tensorplate-common
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 adduser,
Description: TensorPlate shared maintainer-script helpers (V01-E14)
 Ships the shared install-paths / create-users / path-constants
 helpers used by every tensorplate-* package's maintainer scripts so
 the on-device filesystem layout is created consistently regardless
 of which packages are installed first.
 .
 Installing this package alone has no runtime effect; it is pulled in
 automatically by the agent, observability, serving, and CLI packages.

Package: tensorplate-agent
Architecture: any
Pre-Depends:
 ${misc:Pre-Depends},
 tensorplate-common (= ${source:Version}),
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 adduser,
 systemd,
Recommends:
 tensorplate-cli (= ${binary:Version}),
 tensorplate-observability (= ${binary:Version}),
 tensorplate-serving (= ${binary:Version}),
Suggests:
 tensorplate-backend-python-pytorch (>= ${source:Version}),
Description: TensorPlate device agent (V01-E08/E09)
 The agent owns the local control plane for a single TensorPlate device:
 desired-state store, deploy transaction state machine, bundle
 verification, serving-worker supervision, and the local control API.
 .
 The agent binds locally by default (Unix domain socket). It does not
 expose any network endpoint without explicit configuration.

Package: tensorplate-serving
Architecture: any
Pre-Depends:
 ${misc:Pre-Depends},
 tensorplate-common (= ${source:Version}),
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 tensorplate-agent (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: TensorPlate serving worker (V01-E07)
 The serving worker is the v0.1.0 data plane: HTTP loopback inference
 endpoint, request normalization, buffer plane, scheduler, execution
 session, and backend adapters.
 .
 The serving binary is installed under /usr/lib/tensorplate/ but is
 not registered as a systemd service. The agent supervises its
 lifecycle (V01-E09).

Package: tensorplate-observability
Architecture: any
Pre-Depends:
 ${misc:Pre-Depends},
 tensorplate-common (= ${source:Version}),
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 adduser,
 systemd,
Recommends:
 tensorplate-agent (= ${binary:Version}),
 tensorplate-cli (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: TensorPlate observability service (V01-E10)
 Independent heartbeat / health monitor. Starts and runs without the
 agent or serving worker; consumes events from local in-process and
 (post-v0.1.0) Unix-domain-socket producers and exposes a bounded
 status snapshot consumed by `tensorplate status`.

Package: tensorplate-cli
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 tensorplate-common (= ${source:Version}),
Recommends:
 tensorplate-agent (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: TensorPlate operator CLI (V01-E11)
 Single-device operator CLI: `tensorplate deploy`, `status`, `infer`,
 `logs`, `rollback`, `doctor`. Routes through the agent's local
 control API. Installs the binary as /usr/bin/tensorplate.

Package: tensorplate-backend-python-pytorch
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.10),
 python3-pip,
Recommends:
 tensorplate-agent (>= ${source:Version}),
 tensorplate-serving (>= ${source:Version}),
Description: TensorPlate Python/PyTorch backend (V01-E14-F05)
 Separate package providing the Python sidecar backend used for
 SmolVLA / Python-native model bundles. Installs the
 `tensorplate-backend-python-pytorch` entrypoint and a backend
 descriptor consumed by `tensorplate doctor` and the agent deploy
 compatibility check.
 .
 Core TensorPlate packages do not depend on this package. PyTorch
 itself is intentionally not declared as a Debian dependency; it
 must be installed in the Python environment selected by the
 backend descriptor. `tensorplate doctor` reports PyTorch runtime
 status separately.
